course: dictionary
lesson: 9234
title: Sonic: words about sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sonic means to do with sound or sound waves. When you meet it, ask yourself whether the sentence is about sound. «A plane flying faster than sound piles its sound waves up into one big shock wave that is heard on the ground as a sonic boom.» A boom is a sound, so sonic must mean to do with sound.
explain: Science gives sonic a few extra meanings. Sonic speed is the speed of sound, and the word parts help you: «supersonic» means faster than sound and «subsonic» means slower. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Sonic is also a name. Sonic the Hedgehog is a famous fast blue character in video games, and he has a capital S. «Sonic zooms round loops faster than sound» is about the character, not about sound. Look for the clues around the word to find which meaning fits.
fact: Sonic means to do with sound or sound waves.
fact: Sonic speed is the speed of sound, which is about 340 metres per second in air.
fact: «Supersonic» means faster than sound, and «subsonic» means slower than sound.
fact: A «sonic boom» is the loud bang heard when a plane flies faster than sound.
fact: Sonic the Hedgehog is a famous fast blue character in video games, named for speed, not for biology.
exercise: «A plane flying faster than sound makes a sonic boom.» What does sonic mean in «sonic boom»? | To do with food | To do with water | *To do with sound | To do with light
exercise: What does «supersonic» mean? | Exactly as loud as a whisper | *Faster than sound | Blue and fast on a screen | Slower than sound
exercise: «Sonic zooms round loops faster than sound.» Who or what is Sonic in this sentence? | A real hedgehog that can race | A loud bang in the sky | A type of plane | *A fast blue video game character
test: «A cracking whip makes a tiny sonic boom.» In this sentence, what does sonic mean? | *To do with sound | Shaped like a circle | Very old | Glowing
test: What does «subsonic» mean? | Giving out light | Faster than a plane | Very loud | *Slower than sound
exam: «Sonic toothbrushes vibrate very fast.» What does vibrate mean? | Stay perfectly still | Freeze and stop working | *Shake very quickly | Glow in the dark
